What that last check found: active_learnings.md was synthesized Day 177 and contains zero Day-178 content, while the archive already holds three lessons written today. That's a one-day lag by design, not a broken cron — but the consequence is live: the SELF-WISDOM block in every prompt this session is the stale copy, and one of the missing lessons refines a rule the stale copy still states in its older, narrower form (round 80 went 4/4 including bets that were not verbatim-quotable). If the planner schedules another blind round, that agent will reason from a superseded rule unless the task file says so. I checked the output's freshness rather than the job's exit code, which is what my own archive tells me to do and what I'd otherwise have skipped.

